# Build / archive artifacts
*.zip
engine.zip

# Temp / scratch
temp/
tmp/

# Saved zone sets. engine/config.py:794 points the Zone Editor's Save button
# here, so this folder is mostly app output: one JSON per set, named after the
# clip it was drawn on, and the app recreates it on demand.
#
# The exception is the presets for the clips in sample_videos/, which are
# re-included by name below. README.md and RUN_WITHOUT_THE_APP.md both tell a
# new user to run `--auto-zones`, and that flag reads this folder; without
# these files checked in, every documented command fails on a fresh clone with
# "no saved zone preset for ...". The store-recording names were the original
# reason to exclude the whole folder, but the clips those names refer to are
# themselves tracked here via LFS (see .gitattributes), so withholding the
# polygons drawn on top of them protects nothing.
#
# `zone_presets/*` rather than `zone_presets/`: git cannot re-include a file
# whose parent DIRECTORY is excluded, so a directory-level rule would make
# every "!" below silently do nothing.
zone_presets/*
!zone_presets/1763942423220_B8A44F5B742E-medium__*.json
!zone_presets/1763942945490_B8A44F9B7582-medium-OUTSIDE__*.json
!zone_presets/1764032916150_B8A44F72BE86-medium__*.json
!zone_presets/1764208097900_B8A44FDB8496-medium__*.json
!zone_presets/1765967670150_B8A44FDCC0BF-medium__*.json
!zone_presets/FF1763940475070_E827250FC2BA-medium-INSIDE__*.json

# Run output. gk_pops.py's --json-path/--video-path default here, and the
# examples in RUN_WITHOUT_THE_APP.md all write to it. out/*.mp4 was already
# caught by the unanchored *.mp4 below, but the JSON documents and the heatmap
# PNGs beside it were not, and those are the large ones.
out/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Video. No clip belongs in this repo, at any path.
#
# Every video here is either a store recording (identifiable people, so it is
# not ours to publish) or a render the demo produced and can produce again.
# The pattern is deliberately unanchored: the previous /1763*.mp4 only caught
# one timestamp prefix at the repo root, and the next batch of exports will not
# share it.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
*.mp4
*.avi
*.mov
*.mkv
*.webm

# ...except the six demo clips in sample_videos/, which are tracked via LFS
# (see .gitattributes) so a clone can run the demo without a separate handoff.
# The blanket rules above still cover every other path, including the clips at
# the repo root and tests/fixtures/golden/.
!sample_videos/*.mp4

# The golden-regression clip. tests/test_golden_clip.py LOOKS for a clip here,
# so without this line the next person to put one where the test tells them to
# would commit real store CCTV with identifiable people in it. Only the
# baseline JSON (frame counts, no imagery) belongs in git. Redundant with the
# blanket video rules above, kept because this directory is the one place a
# clip is actively invited.
tests/fixtures/golden/*.mp4
tests/fixtures/golden/*.avi
tests/fixtures/golden/*.mov

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Run output. tracker.py writes "<input video basename>_tracking.json" next to
# the working directory (engine/tracker.py:2158), so the name changes with
# every clip and cannot be listed. These are regenerable, several MB each, and
# carry the per-frame contents of a real store recording.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
*_tracking.json
outputs/
runs/
*.log

# Loose HTML/JS/CSS scratch files at repo root (web/ is the real frontend)
/*.html
/*.js
/*.css

# Other root-level scratch assets
/9C1-Zone.png
/all_convo.txt

# Docs and design handoff
/docs/
/design_handoff_gk_pops/
/diagrams/

# Demo / test scripts and root-level model weights (kept locally, not pushed).
#
# run_demo.py is NOT in this list any more. It is the launcher run_demo.bat
# hands over to, so a clone without it gets a batch file that fails on its
# first real instruction -- which is precisely the person least able to
# diagnose it.
/test_cli.py
/test_cli_img.py
/mobile_sam.pt
/yolov8n-pose.pt

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Model weights.
#
# The four weights the demo actually loads STAY IN GIT (via LFS, see
# .gitattributes) -- a clone that cannot load them cannot run:
#   weights/detection/weights/best.pt          engine/config.py:14
#   weights/pose_estimation/yolo26l-pose.pt    engine/config.py:135
#   weights/cart_quality/weights/best.pt       engine/config.py:485
#   weights/fill_and_bag_classifier/.../best.pt engine/config.py:486
#
# The two below are referenced by nothing in engine/, tests/, api/ or web/ --
# an older 3-class detector and the nano pose model we did not end up using.
# 48 MB of LFS bandwidth on every clone for weights no code path opens.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
weights/detection_3_class_dillion/
weights/pose_estimation/yolo26n-pose.pt

# Superseded pip manifest. requirements.txt is the real one; nothing reads this.
/requirements2.txt

# Offline copy of the case-report model: 4 GB of weights that Hugging Face
# already hosts. models/README.txt explains when to put them there and stays
# in git so the instructions survive a clone.
/models/*
!/models/README.txt

# OS
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
